  "scope": "Complete BAM/BED consensus counting through original summarizeOverlaps, explicit LIB/RLE/TMM normalization and full/peak library sizes, additive source-factor contrasts with DESeq2 or edgeR, complete reports including source NULL selection, PCA and uniquely labeled correlation heatmaps through original DiffBind 3.24.0 / R 4.6.2. Single-end, paired-end and shared-control workflows are qualified. Java validates complete input BAM/BED populations and projects fitted DESeq2 rows against the full original namespace; upstream code fits and shrinks models. Complete model/count RDS, reports and PNGs are freshly replayed byte-for-byte. One scoped upstream family; native helpers receive no extra family credit. Historical author editions, inferred formulas/defaults, arbitrary R expressions or input RDS, custom GoodpeaksScript, randomized-pair generation, whole-package equivalence and full-paper reproduction remain unqualified.",
  "required_action": "Require COMPLETED.json, read WARNINGS.md and OUTPUT-AUDIT.json and all original source warnings/logs, then run diffbind-tools --verify with NEW scratch, the exact producing JAR and unchanged bound Linux runtime. Missing or forbidden prerequisites give SKIP3 and skip dependent analysis; supply/install exact prerequisites only where permitted, otherwise retain the skip and required action. FAIL2 admits no complete result: preserve the attempt, correct changed/invalid data/runtime, model failure, capacity exhaustion or cancellation and retry NEW paths. External JVM termination may return a signal exit code; interrupted captures remain incomplete. Original NULL selected reports and their warnings are preserved as valid empty selections, separate from failed models. test_fold changes the original hypothesis test AND report filter; it is not a post-hoc view-only cutoff. Repeated report headers remain ordinal columns. MaxQuant runtime stays skipped and MaxQuant/Andromeda/MaxDIA pending; Cell Ranger remains excluded. Raw XML/process/runtime/cleanup evidence stay private; literature HTMLs remain withheld from Pages. Existing 0.4.1 release downloads predate this source-built command.",
